# Byte-exact protection for the sealed Notanda emblem handoff package.
#
# The package ships manifest.json and SHA256SUMS covering every file with its
# SHA-256 over the unmodified raw bytes. This repository runs with
# core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite LF to CRLF on checkout for the .md,
# .svg, SHA256SUMS and manifest.json files inside the package and break both
# `tools/handoff_manifest.py verify` and `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS`.
#
# Scope is deliberately narrow: only the sealed package directory. Ordinary
# brand documents outside it follow the usual repository rules.
docs/brand/Notanda_Emblem_Final_V1.0_2026-09-11/** -text

# The manifest test harness is a bash script. Under core.autocrlf=true a
# Windows checkout would give it CRLF line endings, which Linux and WSL bash
# reject. Keep it LF everywhere. Scoped to this one file on purpose.
tools/run_handoff_manifest_tests.sh text eol=lf

# The application copies of sealed artwork must also survive checkout byte-for-byte.
src/harvester/webui/static/*.svg -text
src/harvester/webui/static/*.woff2 -text
